//! The `column-height` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property specifies
//! the height of the columns in a [CSS multi-column
//! layout](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Multicol_layout).
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: The initial value. If the content container has a set height, the content columns will
//! grow to that height, overflowing to the side if the content doesn't fit inside the container. If
//! the content container does not have a set height, the content will be equally distributed between
//! the columns generated inside the container.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | <length [0,∞]>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-multicol-2/#propdef-column-height
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/column-height
//!
